<Base title="About" description="The Paper Trail publishes free, plain-English money guides for real families.">
  <section class="page prose">
    <h1>About The Paper Trail</h1>
    <p>The Paper Trail started as a money-stories page followed by thousands of readers who wanted one thing: <strong>money explained like a normal person would explain it.</strong></p>
    <p>This site is the home for our longer guides on budgeting, saving, cutting bills, retirement basics and the history behind everyday prices. Every guide is written to be useful the same day you read it: clear steps, real numbers, no jargon.</p>
    <h2>Who writes this</h2>
    <p>Hi, I'm <strong>Sharon</strong>. I write the guides here, and I run The Paper Trail's money pages. My goal is simple: explain money the way a friend would, with real numbers and no jargon.</p>
    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Simple beats perfect.</strong> A budget you actually follow is better than a perfect one you abandon.</li>
      <li><strong>No hype.</strong> No get-rich-quick tricks, no hot stock picks, no investment tips.</li>
      <li><strong>Show the math.</strong> We use real numbers and check our facts against reliable sources.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Education, not advice</h2>
    <p>Everything here is general education. We are not financial advisors, and nothing on this site is personal financial, tax or legal advice. Read our full <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
    <h2>Say hello</h2>
    <p>Spotted a mistake or have a question you'd like us to answer? Visit the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
